The author steps aside in their own secondary voice — notes, boxed asides, and disclosure.

<section #ag-aside | `<aside>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<aside>`.

<code #code:ag-aside-1>
<aside | A side note about the elephant.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-aside-1>
<aside | A side note about the elephant.>
</minipage>

<section #ag-details | `<details>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<details>`.

<code-block #code:ag-details-1>
<details>
  <summary | More background>
  Additional context for the curious reader. The summary is the
  visible heading; this body shows when the disclosure is opened.
</details>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-details-1>
<details>
  <summary | More background>
  Additional context for the curious reader. The summary is the
  visible heading; this body shows when the disclosure is opened.
</details>
</minipage>

*The canonical shape: a &lt;summary&gt; for the visible heading,
followed by the disclosure body. The body is recursively parsed
as prose / block content.*

<section #ag-endnotes | `<endnotes>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<endnotes>`.

<section #ag-note | `<note>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<note>`.

<code #code:ag-note-1>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-note-1>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</minipage>

<section #ag-note-list | `<note-list>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<note-list>`.

<section #ag-summary | `<summary>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<summary>`.

<code #code:ag-summary-1>
<summary | More background>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-summary-1>
<summary | More background>
</minipage>

*The visible heading of a &lt;details&gt; disclosure. Appears as a
child of &lt;details&gt;.*
